    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <p>I’m [artist name], an artist based in [home city]. My two main mediums are oil paint and pen sketches.</p>
    <p>I paint in oil because it stays wet for days. That gives me time to move colour around, scrape it back and build the surface in layers until the light feels right. Oil lets me work slowly and change my mind, and the brush strokes stay in the finished painting.</p>
    <p>I sketch in pen because it is direct. Ink cannot be rubbed out, so every line has to count, and every mark shows how it was made. Many of my paintings begin as pen sketches.</p>
    <p>I also make prints, cards and postcards, so more people can take a piece home. I paint [subjects the artist paints]. I started in [year started], and I am [training or self-taught].</p>
    <p>Every original here is one of a kind. To ask about a piece or a commission, visit <a class="line-link" href="/commission-contact/">Commission &amp; Contact</a>.</p>
